    "summary": "Textile, of sheep&#039;s wool, woven in tapestry or plain weave, the warp of white wool, and weft of natural brown, and white wool, red analine dyed wool, also grey wool, all single spun, except for a two-ply natural brown &#039;S&#039; twist thread used for selvage. The design consists of a brown ground with a large open key-edged rectangular design in red, with a second geomtric design, in two parts, in the centre. Eight small enclosed areas in the white design are filled with a grey wool.",
